I’m building a user management dashboard with React, Vite, and Tailwind. I have a component called `UserList` that fetches data from `/api/users` and displays each user’s avatar, name, and email. Currently, I’m using `useState` and `useEffect` directly in the component for data fetching, and I store the results in a global Zustand store. The component re-renders every time any state changes, even when unrelated fields are updated. Also, the images are full-size JPEGs.

Could you refactor this component to:
- Use React Query for server state (with proper stale/cache times, e.g., 5 min stale, 10 min cache).
- Keep only truly global client state in Zustand (e.g., selected user ID), but not the raw API response.
- Apply `React.memo` or `useCallback` to avoid unnecessary re-renders.
- Lazy-load the avatar images with `<img loading="lazy" />` and convert to WebP format.
- Wrap the component in an error boundary that shows a fallback UI on fetch failure.
- Ensure the component follows the container/presenter pattern: extract the data-fetching logic into a custom hook called `useUsers`.

Here’s a representative snippet of the current code (you can assume similar structure):

```tsx
// UserList.tsx
import { useUserStore } from '../store/userStore';
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

export default function UserList() {
  const { users, setUsers } = useUserStore();
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('/api/users')
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => {
        setUsers(data);
        setLoading(false);
      });
  }, []);

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;

  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col gap-4">
      {users.map(user => (
        <div key={user.id} className="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 bg-white rounded shadow">
          <img src={user.avatarUrl} alt={user.name} className="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
          <div>
            <p className="font-semibold">{user.name}</p>
            <p className="text-gray-500">{user.email}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

I’d like the final output to be the refactored `UserList` component, the new custom hook `useUsers`, the updated Zustand store (if needed), and an `ErrorBoundary` wrapper component. Also, show how you would lazily import this page using `React.lazy` in the router.
